# A Star of Hope
Tamil title: நம்பிக்கை நட்சத்திரம்

Amid the darkness of anguish, a star of hope is shining! To all our honourable comrades whose eyes brim with tears, a light has become visible: a light that inspires hope that renewal is still possible.

For all the comrades who have spent the past several days sobbing in distress, here is a new consolation, a great medicine for their wounded hearts. News has appeared in *Viduthalai* that will make them exclaim eagerly and joyfully, "Here, here is his statement, the leader's statement!"

On the twenty-eighth, all the newspapers were like a lighthouse appearing in the distance to a vessel that had been caught and battered in a storm.

Newspapers such as *Dinasari*, *Dinamani*, and *Dina Thanthi* also carried Periyar's statement and filled us with joy.

We had been offering our tears as a sacrifice, inwardly believing that they could not fail to bear fruit. Then we saw the newspapers in which Periyar made a moving appeal, saying that his marriage arrangement had distressed the comrades of the organisation and had fostered disgust and bitterness. Our hearts overflowed with delight; we were astonished.

Our tears are being respected. The leader's mind is changing. The old affection and former love are bringing together again the leader and the comrades who writhe like a child scorched by fire. We believe wholeheartedly that the leader's statement is the beginning of a process through which division, difference, and conflict can disappear and we can once again lead the joyful life of a family.

We commend and welcome this good course adopted by Periyar. We praise the upright people who brought him to this position.

With a heart that had melted and in words that melted our hearts, Periyar wrote "Please forgive me" in *Viduthalai*. We would call this the victory of those comrades who shed tears and demonstrated their honour, devotion to principle, and upright resolve to condemn wrongdoing wherever it occurred. Yes, a great change of heart! Our praise goes to the countless comrades of the organisation who expressed their views courageously and openly.

One stage ends with the victory of our tears.

What is the next stage? When we see that the leader's heart has softened, we gain confidence that the next stage too will come very soon.

It was the news of the marriage that stunned the Dravidar Kazhagam. The organisation lies inactive. Its workers have withdrawn and departed.

The leader now understands the extent to which the marriage wounded the hearts of the organisation's comrades. What must he do next? Dissolution of the marriage! Yes, the action prescribed by law for that purpose!

Once he does this, the chasm of difference separating him from us will fill itself in.

Through this action he can make the inactive organisation, which many fear may die, bloom once again. He can do it!

Leader, it is enough that you have made us suffer. Through your statement, sweet as a drop of honey, our anguish is diminishing. We look toward you with eyes in which affection and hope are blossoming. Come! Let us work again! Remove the fetter of this incompatible marriage, which came as an obstruction, came as a flame, and came as something improper; remove the stain and come. We, your children, call you. Come! Do not doubt our goodwill. Do not fail to respect our integrity. We call to you, saying: end the marriage that has immersed us all in suffering.

As a result of the great majority of the organisation's comrades expressing through their tears a dignified condemnation, we obtained the leader's hope-giving statement. Likewise, if the comrades now express their views about the next stage with discipline, dignity, calm, and devotion to principle, victory will certainly be gained in this matter too. Resolve that we shall do what is necessary. See that star of hope appearing there and rejoice! To bring about complete happiness and a new situation...

---NOTES---
The scan confirms the title நம்பிக்கை நட்சத்திரம்; its printed item number is damaged. The article concerns the 1949 crisis over Periyar's marriage arrangement and explicitly advocates lawful dissolution. The fourth and final scan ends mid-sentence, so the translation stops at the same boundary.
